`),sampleAnswer:["The alkane is **propane** ($\\mathrm{C_3H_8}$).","","The molecular ion peak at $m/z = 44$ represents the molecular mass of the alkane, so the compound must have a molar mass of $44\\ \\mathrm{g\\,mol^{-1}}$.","","$$M(\\mathrm{C_3H_8}) = 3 \\times 12 + 8 \\times 1 = 36 + 8 = 44\\ \\mathrm{g\\ mol^{-1}}$$","","This matches propane, which is the only alkane with that molecular mass.","The strong fragment peak at $m/z = 29$ is also consistent with fragmentation of a three-carbon alkane after loss of a $\\mathrm{CH_3}$ group, which supports propane rather than a larger molecule."].join(`
