`),sampleAnswer:["The lone pair on the nitrogen atom accepts a proton ($\\mathrm{H^+}$) from a water molecule, so ethanamine is a Brønsted–Lowry base and water is the acid. The product is the ethylammonium ion:","","$$\\mathrm{CH_3CH_2NH_2(aq) + H_2O(l) \\rightleftharpoons CH_3CH_2NH_3^+(aq) + OH^-(aq)}$$","","Structural formula of the product: $\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CH_2{-}NH_3^+}$, with the nitrogen now bonded to three H atoms and one C atom and carrying a $+1$ charge.","","Check: charge is conserved ($0 + 0 = +1 + (-1)$) and the extra H on nitrogen came from water, which becomes $\\mathrm{OH^-}$."].join(`
