`),sampleAnswer:Imt(i,a),marks:15}}},Pmt=[Mut,Hut,zut,Uut,Vut,Qut,emt,imt,cmt,umt],Emt=[fmt,ymt,kmt,Cmt,_mt],Omt=["DT-DP-12"],Lmt=["ongoing evaluation throughout design and production","criteria for evaluating design solutions","testing and refining prototypes","identifying and resolving design issues during development"],Mmt={id:"design_and_technology/2023/q01",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...Omt],learningTopics:Lmt,generate(t){const e=[3,0,1,2][t],n="To solve design issues as they arise",i=["To set goals","To explore ideas","To establish consumer needs"],a=[];let o=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)a.push(s===e?n:i[o++]);return{question:"What is the primary purpose of ongoing evaluation?",choices:a,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The primary purpose of ongoing evaluation is to solve design issues as they arise.","","Ongoing evaluation is a continuous process throughout the design and production","cycle. It allows designers to identify and address problems at every stage,","rather than only at the beginning or end of a project.","","Setting goals and exploring ideas occur mainly at the beginning of the design","process. Establishing consumer needs is part of the initial research phase.","Ongoing evaluation specifically focuses on monitoring and resolving issues","throughout the entire design process."].join(`
`)}}}},Fmt=["DT-DP-6","DT-DP-3"],Rmt=["selecting materials to suit a design brief","renewable resources and sustainable material choices","sustainability as a factor in material selection"],Bz=["Aesthetics","Availability","Sustainability","Life cycle analysis"],zz=[{stem:["A homewares brand makes its serving trays from cork. The cork is stripped from","the bark of living cork oak trees, which regrow their bark and are never cut down."],answer:"Sustainability",reason:["The reason given is that the material is **renewable**: the trees survive the","harvest and regrow the bark, so the resource is not used up. Choosing a","material for this reason is a sustainability decision.","","Nothing is said about how the trays look or how easy cork is to obtain, and no","study of the product’s whole life from extraction to disposal is described."]},{stem:["A perfume company packages its fragrance in hand-blown coloured glass because","the glowing colours and weight make the bottle look luxurious on the shelf."],answer:"Aesthetics",reason:["The reasons given are all about **appearance and feel**: the colours and the","luxurious look on display. Choosing a material for its visual appeal is an","aesthetic decision.","","Glass may also be recyclable, but that is not why this company chose it."]},{stem:["A boat builder on a remote island makes its dinghies from the plywood sold at","the island’s only hardware supplier, because other boat materials take weeks","to arrive by ferry."],answer:"Availability",reason:["The deciding reason is that plywood is **easy to obtain** locally while other","materials take weeks to arrive. Choosing a material because it can be sourced","reliably and quickly is an availability decision.","","Nothing suggests the plywood was chosen for its looks or its environmental","benefits."]},{stem:["An appliance maker switched its vacuum-cleaner housings from ABS to recycled","polypropylene after measuring the energy, emissions and waste of each option","from raw-material extraction through manufacture, use and disposal."],answer:"Life cycle analysis",reason:["The company compared the materials across **every stage of the product’s life**,","from extraction through manufacture and use to disposal. That systematic","cradle-to-grave comparison is a life cycle analysis, and its results decided","the material.","","Sustainability is the broad goal, but the question asks what determined the","choice, and here the method (the full life cycle assessment) is described","explicitly."]}],Nmt={id:"design_and_technology/2023/q02",version:1,variants:zz.length,syllabusTopics:[...Fmt],learningTopics:Rmt,generate(t){const e=zz[t];return{question:[...e.stem,"","Which factor most influenced the choice of this material?"].join(`
