`),sampleAnswer:["The two lamps produce light in different ways, and this is what the","question is testing.","","- The **sodium lamp** is a gas discharge lamp. Its spectrum is a **line","  emission spectrum**: bright lines at a few particular wavelengths (for","  sodium, a strong yellow pair near 589 nm) on a dark background. Each line","  comes from electrons in sodium atoms dropping between fixed energy levels,","  giving photons of energy $E = hf$ equal to the gap between the levels.","- The **filament globe** has a hot solid filament that behaves roughly like a","  black body. Its spectrum is **continuous**: every visible wavelength is","  present, with no gaps, and the intensity changes smoothly with wavelength.","","A full comparison names both spectrum types and gives the reason for each,","not only a description of one of them."].join(`
