`),choices:i,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The aim of the transmission system is to waste as little energy as possible in the","long lines. The lines have resistance $R$, so the power lost as heat is","","$$P_{\\text{loss}} = I^2 R$$","","For a given power $P = VI$, raising the voltage lowers the current. Because the loss","depends on $I^2$, halving the current cuts the loss to a quarter. So the lines should","carry **high voltage and low current**.","","- At the plant, a **step-up** transformer raises the voltage and lowers the current","  before the energy enters the lines.","- Near the suburb, a **step-down** transformer lowers the voltage to a safe level for","  household use.","","An option with a step-down transformer at the plant cannot give high voltage in the","lines, because that transformer would lower the voltage. An option with high current","and low voltage in the lines would make the $I^2 R$ heating losses very large, even if","the transformers are in the right order."].join(`
