`),choices:n,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["Draw a free-body diagram for each bar.","","**Bar Q (hovering).** Only two forces act on it: its weight $W_Q$ downward and the","magnetic force from P. Q is at rest, so the magnetic force on Q must be **upward**","and equal to $W_Q$. The bars therefore **repel**. Parallel currents repel only when","they flow in **opposite** directions, so the currents cannot be in the same direction.","","**Bar P (on the bench).** By Newton's third law, Q pushes back on P with a magnetic","force of the same size, $W_Q$, but directed **downward**. So the magnetic force on P","is not upward. The forces on P are:","- its weight $W_P$, downward","- the magnetic force from Q, equal to $W_Q$, downward","- the normal force $N$ from the bench, upward","","P is in equilibrium, so","","$$N = W_P + W_Q$$","","The bench supports the weight of **both** bars, even though it only touches P. The","option that says the bench force equals the weight of Q alone leaves out the weight","of P itself."].join(`
